      "writtenOn": "2023-11-13T21:49:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that `TextureSaver` is kind of a AEMU specific function, could we put these into `hardware/google/gfxstream/host/include/gfxstream/virtio-gpu-gfxstream-renderer-goldfish.h`?\n\nI guess my current (potentially naive) expectation is eventually `gfxstream/virtio-gpu-gfxstream-renderer.h` would have a more generic:\n\n```\nint stream_renderer_save_snapshot(uint32_t* size,  uint8_t* data);\nint stream_renderer_load_snapshot(uint32_t size, const uint8_t* data);\n```\n\nwhich works more like the `vkEnumerate*()` functions where you first query the size, then allocate, then actually snapshot. So Qemu/Crosvm would have something like:\n\n```\nuint32_t gfxstream_snapshot_space_needed \u003d 0;\nif (stream_renderer_save_snapshot(\u0026gfxstream_snapshot_space_needed, nullptr)) {\n  // handle error\n}\n\nuint8_t* gfxstream_snapshot_space \u003d \u003cstream-\u003eallocate(gfxstream_snapshot_space_needed) / stream-\u003ereserve(gfxstream_snapshot_space_needed)\u003e ;\n\nif (stream_renderer_save_snapshot(\u0026gfxstream_snapshot_space_needed, gfxstream_snapshot_space)) {\n  // handle error\n}\n\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 243,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "845e65324b071a8b0cca2d10dab309059ebc7403",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
